# [MODULE DOC]
# Tempita template generating sklearn/metrics/_dist_metrics.pyx: the DistanceMetric
# family used throughout scikit-learn (BallTree/KDTree in sklearn.neighbors,
# pairwise-distance reductions in sklearn.metrics._pairwise_distances_reduction,
# HDBSCAN, etc.) and exposed publicly as sklearn.metrics.DistanceMetric.
# Structure:
# - DistanceMetric: dtype-agnostic public facade whose get_metric dispatches to the
#   float64 or float32 specialisation.
# - Inside the Tempita for-loop, everything is instantiated twice, with suffix 64
#   (float64 inputs) and 32 (float32 inputs): METRIC_MAPPING<suffix> (string id ->
#   class), the abstract base DistanceMetric<suffix> and one subclass per metric
#   (Euclidean, SEuclidean, Manhattan, Chebyshev, Minkowski, Mahalanobis, Hamming,
#   Canberra, BrayCurtis, boolean metrics, Haversine, PyFunc).
# - Each metric implements C-level, GIL-free per-vector kernels: dist / rdist on dense
#   vectors and dist_csr / rdist_csr on CSR rows (merge of sorted index lists), plus
#   rdist<->dist conversions. rdist is a cheaper rank-preserving surrogate (e.g.
#   squared Euclidean) used by neighbor searches.
# - The base class provides generic pdist / cdist (dense and CSR) loops and the
#   Python-level pairwise() convenience method used mainly by tests.
# Internal accumulators are float64; results are cast to the input dtype.
# The matching declarations live in _dist_metrics.pxd.tp so other Cython modules can
# cimport these classes and call the kernels without the GIL.
{{py:

implementation_specific_values = [
    # Values are the following ones:
    #
    # name_suffix, INPUT_DTYPE_t, INPUT_DTYPE
    ('64', 'float64_t', 'np.float64'),
    ('32', 'float32_t', 'np.float32')
]

}}
